.TH BRICK 1 "" "brick" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brick \- storage sync CLI client for Webbite Brick
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brick
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR]
.I command
[\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brick
is the command-line client for Webbite Brick's storage sync feature. Its
.B sync
command performs two-way synchronization between a local folder and Brick: it
walks both trees, uploads local-only files, downloads remote-only files, and
resolves conflicts with the remote copy winning. After the initial pass it
watches the local folder for filesystem changes and also polls the Storage
API periodically, so both sides stay in sync until interrupted.
.PP
.B brick
also manages the OIDC login and active account used for sync, and can
transfer a single file or folder outside of the sync loop via its
.B upload
and
.B download
commands.
.PP
On first run
.B brick
creates a configuration file at
.I ~/.config/brick/config.yaml
containing a unique client identifier.
Authentication tokens are stored in the same file after a successful login.
.PP
Global options must precede the command name; a command's own options must
precede its positional arguments. For example:
.B brick \-\-no\-upgrade\-check sync \-d
is valid,
.B brick sync \-d \-\-no\-upgrade\-check
is not.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit. Must be used alone.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version number, build timestamp, and git commit hash, then exit.
Must be used alone.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-upgrade\-check
Suppress the automatic check for a newer version of
.B brick
that normally runs before
.BR sync .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-control\-api
Disable the local status/control API that
.B "brick sync"
otherwise starts alongside the sync loop. Local clients such as a tray app
use this API to query sync status and to send commands (pause, quit,
detach) to a running instance; with this flag such clients cannot find or
control the process.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Print a single line of JSON reporting whether
.B "brick sync"
is expected to succeed right now (login, active account, sync folder, and
API reachability), without starting a sync. Meant for a companion app.
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-and\-exit
Run every interactive step a normal
.B "brick sync"
start would (login, sync-folder selection, first-run onboarding, an API
reachability check), then exit without ever starting a sync. Meant for a
companion app driving brick's setup from its own installer.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Account management
.TP
.B login
Open the default web browser and start login flow.
On completion the received credentials are saved to the configuration file.
Run this command before using any feature that requires an authenticated account.
.TP
.B switch\-accounts
Interactively select which account to make active when more than one account
has been authenticated.
The selected account ID is persisted to the configuration file.
.TP
.B whoami
Print the name, email address, and active account of the currently authenticated
user.
If the access token has expired it is refreshed silently using the stored refresh
token.
.TP
.B restart
Clear existing settings and configure Brick from scratch, as if freshly
installed. Stops any running instance, then for each account with a
configured sync folder interactively offers to delete its local files and
the folder itself, removes the entire configuration directory, and then
immediately re-enters the same interactive setup a foreground
.B sync
would run.
.TP
.B uninstall
Interactively remove the
.B brick
binary, configuration directory, shell completion files, and man page.
Each step prompts for confirmation before proceeding.
.SS "sync \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Synchronizes the folder configured as
.I storageSyncFolder
in the configuration file with Brick, then watches it for changes.
If no sync folder is configured yet,
.B "brick sync"
prompts for one and persists it to the configuration file. The remote copy
always wins on conflict. Requires a logged-in session with an active account
(see
.B login
and
.BR switch\-accounts ).
Press
.B Ctrl\-C
to stop syncing. When run in an interactive terminal, the sync loop also
accepts
.BR D
to detach into the background (equivalent to
.BR \-\-daemon ,
where supported) and
.BR P
to pause or resume syncing without stopping it.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Detach into the background once logged in and Brick's API is reachable,
so syncing continues after the terminal is closed. The same effect can also
be triggered interactively from the foreground sync loop by pressing
.BR D .
Not supported on Windows.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Used together with
.BR \-d .
Print a single line of JSON reporting the outcome of starting the daemon
(or why it failed) instead of running interactively. Meant for a companion
app that starts brick in daemon mode itself.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote\-control
Allow Brick to remotely list, browse, and transfer files on this device while
syncing. Without this flag the local agent refuses any such request from Brick,
even if it is otherwise connected. Can also be enabled persistently via the
configuration file, in which case this flag is unnecessary.
.TP
.B \-\-agent\-root \fIPATH\fR
Expose an additional directory (beyond
.IR storageSyncFolder )
to remote clients when
.B \-\-remote\-control
is enabled. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-selective\-sync
Interactively choose which top-level folders of the active account are
excluded from sync. Folders newly excluded are deleted from local disk
immediately; any running
.B brick
instance is restarted to pick up the change.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-selective\-sync
Print the folders currently excluded from sync for the active account.
.SS "upload \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR|\fIdir\fR [\fItarget\-path\fR|\fIuuid\fR]"
Upload a local file or folder to Brick, outside of the two-way sync loop.
.I target
may be a remote path (created if it doesn't already exist, like
.BR "mkdir \-p" )
or a folder's UUID; if omitted, the upload goes to the account root.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Required when the source is a folder; without it brick does nothing and
exits non\-zero rather than guessing the whole tree was intended.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Suppress the pre\-flight summary, per\-file progress bars, and final summary
line. Errors are still printed.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
If a file with the same name already exists at the destination, replace its
content instead of creating a copy (Brick's default behavior otherwise, e.g.
.IR "report.pdf" " \(-> " "report (copy).pdf" ).
.SS "download \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIuuid\fR|\fIpath\fR [\fItarget\-dir\fR]"
Download a remote file or folder from Brick, outside of the two-way sync
loop.
.I source
may be a node UUID or a remote path.
.I target\-dir
defaults to the current directory if omitted, and is created if it doesn't
already exist. An existing local file with the same name is overwritten.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Required when the source is a folder; without it brick does nothing and
exits non\-zero rather than guessing the whole tree was intended.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Suppress the pre\-flight summary, per\-file progress bars, and final summary
line. Errors are still printed.
.PP
Both
.B upload
and
.B download
continue past a per\-file error during a recursive transfer rather than
aborting; every failure is listed at the end, and the process exits non\-zero
if any occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Log in to a Webbite account:
.EX
brick login
.EE
.TP
Show the currently authenticated user:
.EX
brick whoami
.EE
.TP
Switch to a different account:
.EX
brick switch\-accounts
.EE
.TP
Sync the configured folder with Brick and watch for changes:
.EX
brick sync
.EE
.TP
Sync and allow Brick to remotely browse and transfer files:
.EX
brick sync \-\-remote\-control
.EE
.TP
Sync without checking for CLI upgrades first:
.EX
brick \-\-no\-upgrade\-check sync
.EE
.TP
Sync and immediately detach into the background:
.EX
brick sync \-\-daemon
.EE
.TP
Choose which folders to exclude from sync:
.EX
brick sync \-\-selective\-sync
.EE
.TP
List folders currently excluded from sync:
.EX
brick sync \-\-list\-selective\-sync
.EE
.TP
Clear all local settings and set up Brick again from scratch:
.EX
brick restart
.EE
.TP
Upload a folder recursively to a remote path:
.EX
brick upload \-r ~/Photos /Backups/Photos
.EE
.TP
Download a remote folder by UUID into the current directory:
.EX
brick download \-r 3fa85f64\-5717\-4562\-b3fc\-2c963f66afa6
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/brick/config.yaml
Per-user configuration file.
Created automatically on first run.
Contains the client identifier, the configured
.IR storageSyncFolder ,
and, after login, OAuth credentials.
Stored with mode
.B 0600
to protect the tokens.
Do not share this file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/brick/sync\-state\-<account\-id>.json
Per-account sync state index, one file per account ID ever synced (so two
accounts sharing the same local folder still keep independent bookkeeping).
Records the last-known local hash and remote ETag for each synced file, plus
a server-time cursor for incremental polling, so repeated runs only transfer
what changed. Safe to delete;
.B "brick sync"
will simply re-reconcile the full tree on the next run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (invalid flags, network failure, authentication error,
one or more files failed during a recursive transfer, etc.).
